cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Governance Kernel in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "Governance Kernel: A deterministic governance layer for AI agents"
abstract: >-
  Governance Kernel is a deterministic governance layer that
  runs before AI agents act. Unlike post-hoc monitoring
  approaches, the kernel decides permissions, trust levels,
  and resource bounds before any agent action is executed.
  The kernel provides separation of concerns (information /
  policy / node), signed policies, a hash-chained audit log,
  a kill switch, a resource governor, and multi-agent
  consensus primitives. It is verified across three
  environments (Termux, GitHub Actions CI, Google Colab)
  and includes pre-registered thresholds and a reproducible
  benchmark suite (V0.4: 54/54, PRI = 1.0000).
